// CONSTRIQ — Construction Profit Intelligence & Project Financial Control
//
// North star:
//   Expected Profit → Forecast Profit → Profit at Risk → Why? → Action
//
// Non-negotiable financial rules (enforced by this model + application transactions):
//   1. No double counting: Actual, open commitment, and forecast-to-complete are mutually exclusive.
//   2. Submitted variation is not revenue. Only approved/executed variations post to expected revenue.
//   3. Original budget is historical and must remain visible after revisions.
//   4. Current budget is separate; approved revisions change current, never original.
//   5. Every actual cost is attributable, or flagged unallocated.
//   6. Forecast-to-complete is uncommitted remaining cost only (not actual, not open commitment).
//   7. Profit at risk = expected profit − forecast profit and must be stored explicitly.
//   8. Material financial changes are auditable; history is reversed, not silently overwritten.
//   9. Revenue and cost are separate; raising the cost budget never increases expected revenue.
//  10. Health labels must be explained by ranked leakage findings.

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
}

